    "lawCode": "Amd §2.10, CP L",
    "lawSection": "Criminal Procedure Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8672A\n\nSPONSOR: COONEY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the criminal procedure law, in relation to designating\nas peace officers certain employees of the Monroe county sheriff's\noffice serving as court security deputies at Monroe county court facili-\nties\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nProvides peace officer status to court security deputies, employed by\nthe Monroe County Sheriff's Department at Monroe County court facili-\nties.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1. Section 2.10 of the criminal procedure law is amended by\nadding a new subdivision 86 to allow a deputy sheriff who is employed by\nthe sheriff's department of Monroe county to perform the delivery of\nsecurity services to the courts.\n\nSection 2 establishes the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe New York State Office of Court Administration (OCA) contracts and\npays for court security personnel in the Hall of Justice, Rochester, New\nYork. OCA requires that all such personnel be certified and registered\nwith the Bureau of Municipal Police. OCA has recommended Monroe County\nto seek special legislation to allow county sheriff deputies to perform\ncourt security services.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2019-2020: S.3808\n\n2017-2018: S.8916/A.985 - Passed both houses\n\n2013-2014:  S.4892A/A.3765A - Passed both houses\n\n2011-2012: S.5454/A.720 - passed senate\n\n2009-2010: S.4195/A.2278\n\n2007-2008: S.548/A.779\n\n2005-2006: S.1271a/A.364a\n\n2003-2004: S.3525/A.1048 - passed assembly\n\n2001-2002:S.4521/A.99a - passed assembly\n\n2000: S.7156a/A.10928a - passed senate\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the thirtieth day after it shall have\nbecome a law.\n",
